  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1137 AM CST THU NOV 26 2026\n\nMoisture wrapping around the upper low will bring a few batches\nof light rain this afternoon into tonight, especially across the\nnorth, with only low rain chances farther south. As colder air\narrives this evening, a brief rain/snow mix is possible across\nthe far northern counties through midnight. No accumulation is\nexpected, since precipitation will be light and ground\ntemperatures remain warm. Breezy west to northwest winds will\nhold temperatures steady in the upper 30s to mid 40s this\nafternoon before they begin falling by late afternoon. Lingering\nclouds and a steady west wind will keep temperatures warmer\ntonight than they would otherwise be, with lows in the 30s.\n\nSkies clear Friday, and with lighter winds, lows fall into the\nmid 20s to mid 30s Saturday morning. Southerly flow returns\nSaturday, warming highs about 10 degrees into the low 60s.\nAnother upper trough sends a cold front through the area on\nSunday, with a 70-80% chance of rain and a few thunderstorms\npossible, mainly during the day. Instability looks limited, so\nstrong to severe storms are not expected at this time. Rain ends\nSunday evening, followed by drier and cooler weather Monday.\n\n16",
